<rml>
<head>
	<title>Kanturu info (CKanturuInfoWindow)</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="kanturu_info.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="kanturu_info">
	<!-- The Kanturu boss-battle HUD (CKanturuInfoWindow): the frame, the characters and the
	     monsters (or the boss) left, and the time left in newui_number1 digits with a blinking
	     colon. A LayoutMode::Hud window, so .screen is the 640x480 reference screen stretched
	     W/640 x H/480 like the original and #panel sits at the window's reference position. Text
	     does not stretch: it takes the native bold size and cancels the stretch. In the background
	     context, behind its other documents (the original drew it under every panel). Takes no
	     pointer events. -->
	<div class="screen" data-style-transform="'scale(' + scale_x + ', ' + scale_y + ')'">
		<div id="panel" data-style-left="panel_x + 'px'" data-style-top="panel_y + 'px'">
			<div id="back"></div>
			<span class="info-text" id="users" data-style-font-size="bold_text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">{{users_text}}</span>
			<span class="info-text" id="monsters" data-style-font-size="bold_text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">{{monsters_text}}</span>
			<span class="info-text" id="colon" data-if="colon_visible" data-style-font-size="bold_text_px + 'px'"
			      data-style-transform="'scale(' + inverse_scale_x + ', ' + inverse_scale_y + ')'">:</span>
			<img class="digit" src="../../../newui_number1.tga" data-for="d : digits" data-attr-rect="d.rect"
			     data-style-left="d.left + 'px'"/>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
